{
  "_help": [
    "collections: Internet Archive collections searched.",
    "categories: an item is listed under the FIRST category (in this order) whose terms it matches, so specific categories come before broad ones.",
    "terms: words/phrases matched against titles and IA subject tags; write \"double quotes\" inside the string for an exact phrase.",
    "example / contributes: what to collect and why (documentation only; the search ignores them).",
    "optional per category: subject_tags (IA tags only), exclude (title words that rule an item out), candidates, min_minutes, max_minutes, from_date, to_date (YYYY, YYYY-MM or YYYY-MM-DD), stations (channel identifier prefixes), max_mb.",
    "the category name becomes the corpus/<category>/ folder.",
    "Expansion v2: search terms are high-precision format indicators. Broad topical words are excluded because subject tags can produce false positives.",
    "Category-level candidates=150 is a target; adjust global CLI --candidates according to script precedence.",
    "Duration bounds are discovery limits, not acceptance rules. Classification is still first-match, not verified ground truth.",
    "Review selected titles/metadata before downloads; use IA identifier to deduplicate across seeds and rounds."
  ],
